## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant inference, per-tenant SLAs, and practical routing inside an MME while keeping data in a VPC.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Multi-Model Endpoint and on-demand loading
- Per-tenant routing and model versioning
- Auto Scaling and canary rollouts by tenant
- Drift detection, validation, data residency

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example: per-request routing to specific model on an MME
const { SageMakerRuntimeClient, InvokeEndpointCommand } = require("@aws-sdk/client-sagemaker-runtime");
const client = new SageMakerRuntimeClient({region:'us-east-1'});
async function infer(endpoint, modelName, payload){
  return await client.send(new InvokeEndpointCommand({
    EndpointName: endpoint,
    ContentType: 'application/json',
    Accept: 'application/json',
    Body: JSON.stringify({ instances: [payload], modelName })
  }));
}
``

## Why This Is Asked
Tests multi-tenant orchestration, real-time streaming inference, private isolation via PrivateLink, and drift-aware canaries across tenants.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker Model Registry and Pipelines for per-tenant versioning
- PrivateLink and VPC isolation
- Per-tenant feature gating and rate limiting
- Drift detection using per-tenant feature distributions (Feature Store) and latency metrics
- Canary rollout governance with automatic rollback
- Cost modeling per tenant and region

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing and canary logic per tenant
function chooseModelForTenant(tenantId, payload) {
  const meta = loadTenantMeta(tenantId);
  const useCandidate = meta.canaryActive && Math.random() < meta.canaryTraffic;
  const model = useCandidate ? meta.candidateModel : meta.currentModel;
  return model.predict(payload);
}
```

